  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Quality and Production of Leather Bags in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MYOMY do goods designs and sells sustainable and fair trade leather bags and is one of few companies in the fashion industry that is a member of the WFTO. Because of high demand, the need to spread risks and reaching the maximum capacity of its main partner in India, the company was looking for a second production partner. This search led to Bangladesh due to its role as a fashion manufacturer as well as recent misconducts and accidents in the industry which MYOMY do goods aims to address through its business model. After explorative meetings with Leatherina, DGGF-TA provided support to test and improve production capacity of Leatherina, find adequate tanneries that comply with worldwide sustainability standards, assess feasibility of a joint-venture and offer guidance and advise to meet international standards to produce for and export to the European market. For this second project, DGGF-TA has supported to increase the quality of samples and shipments in order to compete with the existing high end brands and to grow her impact. 3 collections have been financed and support has been provided for the WFTO certification process. During this project 45 indirect jobs were supported at Leatherina, of which 75% is female employees. All staff has been trained on quality of the production process and products, the owner of Leatherina has been trained on the WFTO certification process.</narrative>
  </description>
